    "The railway station is one of the most important on the TransPennine route. Trains reach Leeds and Manchester in around half an hour, and local services run to Wakefield, Sheffield via the Penistone line, and the Colne Valley. The line is being rebuilt as part of a long-term upgrade, and disruption and cancellations have been common during construction.",
    "Many people working in Huddersfield live in the town itself or its western suburbs, such as Marsh, Lindley and Edgerton, which offer substantial stone houses at low rents. Holmfirth, Honley and the Colne Valley villages are popular with those who want countryside, although they usually require a bus or car commute.",
    "Buses from across Kirklees converge on the town centre, and road access from the M62 is good. Parking in the centre is relatively affordable compared with larger cities. Commuting from Leeds or Manchester is realistic by train, and living in Huddersfield and working in either city is increasingly common, especially for people who want lower rents and access to the Pennines. The Colne Valley line also serves Slaithwaite and Marsden, stone villages where the moors begin at the end of the street.",
